Re-architected `@561-group/web-theming` from "a Theme is `{head,header,footer,wrap,css}` where `css` is an opaque per-site string" into a real theming system, the way Hugo/Astro/WordPress/Style-Dictionary give you one.
The contract stayed **additive** â€” every new capability is a new optional export; `{name, head, header, footer, wrap, css}` is untouched, so the ~10 dependents kept compiling.
